i guess its all just a matter of perspective.  ive played this game for at 
least 20 years with a very minimal amount of spoiling.  so by some standards 
i think the way most people ascend is based on 'cheating'.  i hadnt even 
invoked wizard/debug mode until just last week.  (first thing i did was wish 
for a sink and boots of speed so i could kick it til the ring dropped lol. 
i would have never had the patience/OCD needed to find that one out without 
a spoiler)  that said at one time i wrote a front end to manage save files 
so i could test some things out.  i certainly 'cheated' there.

i did beat rogue with savefiles just to see what happened once, but i dont 
count that.  although in retrospect it was still quite a feat for an 
unspoiled player and still took several months to finally complete.  now 
that im getting older i figure the only way to cross the 'ascend in nethack' 
item off my lifelist before i croak is to do it the way everyone else does 
it.

but now i have read the spoilers.  just barely scratched them really.  and 
in doing so ive decided two things.

a) if i had continued unspoiled, i would have never ascended in the current 
version of nethack.  probably never even in an old version of rogue.  if for 
no other reason, some crucial steps in the process (particularly in current 
versions of nethack) seem virtually impossible to ever consider doing 
without reading spoilers.

b)  if you want to ascend, the game isnt really what i thought it was.  its 
not about your character learning about the world and applying that to the 
dungeon as i had played for years.  its about YOU learning about the GAME 
and applying it to your character.

ultimately as long as you're having fun i say play how you like.

whos the Best?  the guy who has the most fun.  or maybe the guy who has 
caused the least amount of damage to items in the vicinity after YASD <g>

